WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.938
A Node.

00:00:00.938 --> 00:00:06.388
js application's attack surface begins where untrusted data crosses into trusted application logic.

00:00:06.388 --> 00:00:10.999
Request handlers, routes, controllers, middleware, body parsers, file upload handlers, cookies,

00:00:10.999 --> 00:00:13.094
headers, query strings, route parameters,

00:00:13.094 --> 00:00:18.544
and API payloads all shape what the application believes about the outside world.

00:00:18.544 --> 00:00:22.316
Each boundary deserves an explicit decision about validation, authorization,

00:00:22.316 --> 00:00:23.574
and error handling.

00:00:23.574 --> 00:00:26.508
The runtime surface is broader than HTTP.

00:00:26.508 --> 00:00:29.861
Environment variables may contain secrets, feature flags, URLs,

00:00:29.861 --> 00:00:31.119
and deployment-specific behavior.

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:35.730
File system access can expose paths, temporary files, uploads, generated reports,

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:36.568
and configuration.

00:00:36.568 --> 00:00:41.598
Child processes can turn a small input-handling mistake into a system-level risk

00:00:41.598 --> 00:00:43.694
if command construction is unsafe.

00:00:43.694 --> 00:00:48.724
Network calls can expose internal services when outbound requests are not controlled.

00:00:48.724 --> 00:00:52.497
Data stores and third-party integrations also extend the surface.

00:00:52.497 --> 00:00:57.108
Database queries, object storage, queues, caches, background jobs, webhooks, payment APIs,

00:00:57.108 --> 00:00:57.946
identity providers,

00:00:57.946 --> 00:01:03.395
and notification systems all receive or produce data that may affect security decisions.

00:01:03.395 --> 00:01:09.683
A background job may run outside the normal request path but still process user-controlled content.

00:01:09.683 --> 00:01:15.132
Logs may look passive, yet they can expose sensitive information if treated casually.

00:01:15.132 --> 00:01:20.581
A useful mental model is to trace every path from input to effect.

00:01:20.581 --> 00:01:22.258
Where does data enter?

00:01:22.258 --> 00:01:23.516
What transforms it?

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:25.192
What policy checks happen?

00:01:25.192 --> 00:01:26.869
What service receives it?

00:01:26.869 --> 00:01:28.126
What is logged?

00:01:28.126 --> 00:01:29.803
What happens on failure?

00:01:29.803 --> 00:01:32.318
This view keeps the conversation grounded.

00:01:32.318 --> 00:01:36.510
Security is not only about one route or one library.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:40.702
It is about how trust moves through the whole Node.

00:01:40.702 --> 00:01:41.540
js service.
